		{"id":"a68b2921bfae2940","type":"text","text":"==>","x":-600,"y":-110,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"73677e7689b3a5f1","type":"file","file":"paage22.png","x":-80,"y":-360,"width":400,"height":250},
		{"id":"c0167eb78f1664a8","type":"text","text":"033","x":-600,"y":-480,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"b7102e4d307b61a3","type":"text","text":"034","x":-80,"y":-480,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"39a4f75d09fb0f17","type":"text","text":"What???","x":-600,"y":-420,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"6bd71d8a9fe989b3","type":"text","text":"==>","x":-80,"y":-420,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"c05187befd08ebf1","type":"file","file":"glirp.png","x":480,"y":-360,"width":400,"height":250},
		{"id":"f225d950618d84fe","type":"text","text":"First Contact","x":-80,"y":160,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"61b8e9527941ace8","type":"text","text":"035","x":480,"y":-480,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"d549e23cc9f1c907","type":"text","text":"First Contact","x":480,"y":-420,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"1f6d2e0b8f225131","type":"text","text":"Global News","x":480,"y":400,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"8a70156c3535fd83","type":"file","file":"globalnews.png","x":1040,"y":-360,"width":400,"height":250},
		{"id":"c6cb893400fe6867","type":"text","text":"036","x":1040,"y":-480,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"fb4a03254f215aa0","type":"text","text":"Global News","x":1040,"y":-420,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"78d750f4993aebb5","type":"text","text":"When the GlorpGlirp discovery made its way to global news, people watched with awe what type of wonders their solar system held and was happy about their newfound neighbors in space but was also saddened by the no-contact rule, although they understood its importance.","x":1040,"y":-110,"width":400,"height":270},
		{"id":"2dfee7712fc8b15f","type":"text","text":"Some people still hope","x":1040,"y":160,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"dcba31082ad52140","type":"file","file":"Pasted image 20241110092322.png","x":1620,"y":-352,"width":400,"height":242},
		{"id":"aa75b597dd850fa2","type":"text","text":"037","x":1620,"y":-472,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"b7019c6cd3f86fd7","type":"text","text":"Some people still hope","x":1620,"y":-412,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"4214da841f0675d4","type":"text","text":"Some poeple still hope, hope that Glirpibbles DO want to make contact, but only with a small select few. And they hope that they are that select few, patiently waiting... for a signal","x":1620,"y":-110,"width":400,"height":270},
		{"id":"367a6c5a41bae8d0","type":"text","text":"[Hope]","x":1620,"y":160,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"75fbd57d659e2e4b","type":"text","text":"038","x":-620,"y":560,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"cf03dde82c8cb4ba","type":"text","text":"Hope insan dediğimiz de erenalp yani","x":-620,"y":620,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"639e03881764e4da","type":"file","file":"zackcoming.png","x":-620,"y":680,"width":400,"height":300},
		{"id":"4418885c268319a3","type":"text","text":"Darkness, is what they were used to. So much so that the light that was slowly approaching didn't register in their mind until that same light called out to them.\n\nThe Light: \"Hang on!\"","x":-620,"y":980,"width":400,"height":180},
		{"id":"044073b211936503","type":"text","text":"Dark Green Light ==>","x":-620,"y":1160,"width":400,"height":80},
		{"id":"20a381bf691902cf","type":"text","text":"039","x":-20,"y":560,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"21e51ce284fa9e93","type":"text","text":"040","x":580,"y":560,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"1cc63b49b524985e","type":"text","text":"041","x":1160,"y":560,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"c3fe131eada68956","type":"text","text":"043","x":2360,"y":560,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"9c6c4a46cb6de781","type":"text","text":"044","x":3000,"y":560,"width":400,"height":63},
		{"id":"1a47f99120f7b481","type":"text","text":"In 1955,  Soviet Union and The United States were competing in what is now remembered as the space race. The two mega Nations were competing to see who could send humans farther into the solar system.  In April of that year, The United States became the first Nation to successfully send a human bearing spaceship to the close neighbor of earth, Pehostla. ","x":-80,"y":-110,"width":400,"height":270},
		{"id":"d876c0af6f768ea6","type":"text","text":"The United States Astronauts were surprised to find out that the planet Pehostla housed super intelligent life forms called the Glirpglorps. The Glirpians were peaceful creatures and told the Austranauts they could live with them for a short while before they went back to Earth. In this time the Glirpibbles and Austronauts shared food, culture, music, traditions, and more. When the Astronatus were ready to go back, the Glirpkitties shared a most saddening fact, the no-contact rule. The Glorpians discoverd that the best way to maintain peace with alien species were to not have contact, at all. Earth agreed and a decision was made that each others existence would be acknowledged but the two planets would promise to not interact with each other.","x":480,"y":-110,"width":400,"height":510},
		{"id":"2693134623cc2646","type":"text","text":"046","x":4240,"y":560,"width":400,"height":63},
		{"id":"f2ea0568a1bf2d72","type":"text","text":"047","x":4780,"y":560,"width":400,"height":63},
		{"id":"9a23e6a7b60dcf0d","type":"file","file":"Unsaved Image 1 2.jpg","x":5360,"y":677,"width":400,"height":300},
		{"id":"97f86ee49246510c","type":"file","file":"Unsaved Image 1 3.jpg","x":5920,"y":677,"width":400,"height":300},
		{"id":"360f7fc4fe48c5ea","type":"text","text":"Zoom in ==>","x":5360,"y":620,"width":400,"height":57},
		{"id":"64f94cef1f1e1739","type":"text","text":"Eri was drawing a picutre of the group in what seemed like medival clothing fighting a monster.\n\nEri: I hope this is what Vburb will be like. Maybe we find some loot and fight monsters.\n\nDusty: I don't even know. I'm just happy we get to do something together again. \n\nEri: What do you think it'll be, like what will the compass lead to.\n\nDusty: Maaan i don't knowww. It could lead to nothing, we aren't sure what the alien game entails. Maybe it just leads to a normal tree that aliens think is fun, we can't even read the manual.\n\nEri: Aegis was trying. I'm still not sure if he's telling the truth about this machine coming out of a meteor.\n\nDusty: So what aegis made it all up? Made some technology to create magical items.\n\nEri: well... i donno....","x":5360,"y":977,"width":400,"height":760},
		{"id":"cd0cd31cabb71080","type":"text","text":"In another room ==>","x":5360,"y":1737,"width":400,"height":63},
		{"id":"3ffd6f95560c8863","type":"text","text":"Meanwhile in another room","x":4240,"y":620,"width":400,"height":57},
		{"id":"1e2b0aae056b8f7b","type":"file","file":"Unsaved Image 1.jpg","x":4240,"y":677,"width":400,"height":300},
		{"id":"81a561451d0927ef","type":"text","text":"Zoom in ==>","x":4820,"y":620,"width":400,"height":57},
		{"id":"c78bf1861ce7e208","type":"file","file":"Unsaved Image 1 1.jpg","x":4820,"y":677,"width":400,"height":300},
		{"id":"b381b224be7466b0","type":"text","text":"1:32 AM ","x":3580,"y":620,"width":400,"height":57},
		{"id":"5ef89773d481c90c","type":"file","file":"masa.jpg","x":3580,"y":677,"width":400,"height":300},
		{"id":"a1b3a7e63680baed","type":"text","text":"YUSUF, ERENA, BAZLI, PEL\n\nCoy: We should really sleep soon, it's getting late. I'm sure Apollo will wake us up early for the adventure anyways. \n\nAegis: Yeah, I don't think I could sleep if I laid down right now. I am too excited. I mean... even just the fact that we are finally together again. All of us I mean. It's been months since we did a 'grandma's house'\n\nJoseph: Well we are growing up. Most of us have moved away farther and farther and are following different paths. It's hard to plan stuff like this when you're not an unemployed middle schooler. \n\nAegis: I wish we could just be like how we were. I'm scared that if we grow farther and farther apart eventually we'll just...\n\nPel: Yaaa sacmalama, we keep talking over videochat and playing video games online. We'll be fine. Also, thinking about how sad it is when we are not together while we ARE together isn't helpful. We are together now. Dusty and Apollo haven't argued for once, we are preparing for a big fun adventure tomorrow. This is as good as it gets. \n\nAegis: You're right. I am a homosexual.","x":3580,"y":977,"width":400,"height":773},
		{"id":"7d73b66fab9b86fe","type":"text","text":"Meanwhile in another room ==>","x":3580,"y":1750,"width":400,"height":90},
		{"id":"9a752bac6094f234","type":"text","text":"Apollo and Tarda were working. In secret.\n\nApollo: So how do you center the div again? \n\nTarda: Dude just set the left and right margins to auto, go watch a html tutorial or something.\n\nApollo: I got it, it's so funny how they don't even know we are working on Vstuck this whole time, we just have to finish the art and we'll be golden.\n\nTarda: Don't say it so loud they'll hear you.\n\nApollo: Dude this next page is good, it's gonna be Dusty and Eri speaking, so it's like we are all having different conversations at the same time.\n\nTarda: Just make sure it sounds natural and like them, we don't want another Gambler Pel incident.\n\nApollo: True that.","x":4240,"y":977,"width":400,"height":640},
		{"id":"ac3420a5f530ead9","type":"text","text":"Zoom in ==>","x":4240,"y":1617,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"8f79420ac647e087","type":"text","text":"Get Late","x":2940,"y":617,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"0b26a52c3567b243","type":"file","file":"weather.jpg","x":2940,"y":677,"width":400,"height":300},
		{"id":"9e380f9092f722ff","type":"text","text":"1:32 AM ==>","x":2940,"y":977,"width":400,"height":80},
		{"id":"e3664368dd4cbcb5","type":"text","text":"Contents","x":2380,"y":617,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"18a674a14e4d0396","type":"file","file":"contents.png","x":2380,"y":677,"width":400,"height":300},
		{"id":"77402777b58659c6","type":"text","text":"The box was opened. In it were 3 items. A game manual, a compass, and a countdown timer that had seemingly started counting down from 48 hours the second it was created. The manual had cryptic letters on it and the compass was pointing to an arbitrary direction.\n\nTarda carefully lifted all the contents and put them on the table, looking around in the box for more but there didn't seem to be more.\n\nAegis went up to the cryptic manual and pulled out a notebook titled \"Language of the stars\" In it were different alphabets and ciphers.\n\nThere were some flat stares that seemed to say 'here he goes with his alien obsession' but also an understanding to not interfere. The machine did fall in a meteor so who was to say it ~wasn't~ alien.\n\nApollo: I was really hoping for magical real life dnd \n\nCoy: Same here. But this doesn't even seem to be playable, I mean... a cryptic manual, a compass, and a timer...\n\nPongo: GUYS! It's like a scavenger hunt, and we get treasure at the end! We have to do this.\n\nIt was getting late, there was a moment of silence where they all looked at each other, nodding, shrugging. There was understanding, it was too late for adventure.\n\nEveryone: Nahhhhhhh\n\nApollo: Well then, we leave at first dawn!\n\n","x":2380,"y":977,"width":400,"height":1040},
		{"id":"33b2cc6fb3ea0fa5","type":"text","text":"Get Late ==>","x":2380,"y":2017,"width":400,"height":80},
		{"id":"f9e9f0914cf53c78","type":"text","text":"The item","x":1740,"y":617,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"6ae27a627e55e282","type":"file","file":"Unsaved Image 4.jpg","x":1740,"y":677,"width":400,"height":300},
		{"id":"154a1d71d9f66409","type":"text","text":"On the table stood a box. It looked like a board game, with the name being VBURB.\n\nTarda: Hm\nApollo: So it's a board game! Like the best thing ever for us! \n\nPeople have started getting back up and looking at the box and it was obvious everybody wanted to see the contents so Tarda lifted up the cover.\n","x":1740,"y":977,"width":400,"height":300},
		{"id":"8dd4e2cb17d38807","type":"text","text":"Contents ","x":1740,"y":1277,"width":400,"height":80},
		{"id":"799ea51270be8aa2","type":"text","text":"==>","x":1160,"y":617,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"2afc6bb6ab15d63b","type":"file","file":"Unsaved Image 3.jpg","x":1160,"y":677,"width":400,"height":300},
		{"id":"80c20b801c44104f","type":"text","text":"The energy released from the dark green light was so strong that it pushed people back making them fall on the ground. \n\nAegis: Is everybody okay? Anyone hurt?\n\nThey all looked around and nodded to each other giving an air of understanding that nobody was hurt. There was a moment of silence, of amazement in people's eyes. This moment was abruptly broken by Apollo and Tarda running up to the table to see what had appeared.","x":1160,"y":977,"width":400,"height":320},
		{"id":"a53bc859bc252a6f","type":"text","text":"The item?","x":1160,"y":1297,"width":400,"height":80},
		{"id":"e2bf9909c4ca9a33","type":"text","text":"==>","x":560,"y":977,"width":400,"height":80},
		{"id":"3b56bba96822e6c7","type":"text","text":"Dark green light","x":-20,"y":620,"width":400,"height":60},
		{"id":"59a3ab94e9a24c2c","type":"file","file":"Unsaved Image 1 5.jpg","x":-20,"y":680,"width":400,"height":300},
